-- title:
--   Uniform remainder along a horizontal segment
-- statement:
--   Let $K,N\ge1$, $t\in\mathbb R\setminus\{0\}$, and real $x_l,x_h,\sigma_s,Q,R$
--   satisfy $x_l+2K>0$, $x_h\le\sigma_s$, $-x_l\le\sigma_s$, $Q\ge0$,
--   $\operatorname{pochNormSq}(\sigma_s,t,2K+1)\le Q^2$, and $N^{-x_l}\le R$.
--   Then every $x\in[x_l,x_h]$ satisfies
--   $$|\zeta(x+it)-\operatorname{emFinite}(K,x+it,N)|\le
--   \frac{C_KQR}{N^{2K}(x_l+2K)},$$
--   where $C_K$ is the defined remainder constant. This bounds a whole contour segment.
-- source:
--   https://github.com/DrMurphyIsIn/Arda/blob/af4fde8972eb6d4e78c7d9a95933b18b81adf52d/telperion/examples/zeta_reflection/lean/H1000Octant.lean#L293-L348

